PW H3O+ (nelec_delta -1) with native SCCS, the water-cation preset and 2D PCC along +y: charged
sqrt-CG with the PCC correction in the preconditioner, the far-field Gauss check, and the ENVIRON
monopole constant -pi*Q/(3*L_y) without a Gaussian ionic-shape energy; energy, potential and
ionic force. The former polarization-charge fixed point did not converge for this system.

Reference provenance (regenerated 2026-09-29, ecutwfc 100 Ry / ecutrho 400 Ry):
- ABACUS source commit: 967753df6 (Environ lowpass with exact PCC cavity derivative);
  the default PCC cavity potential now uses the Environ FFT gradient
- ABACUS version: v3.11.0-beta10
- executable SHA256: e204808624109bbf6fa02babe1eab38035133714483206bebb4835e82c696c66
- parallel layout: 16 MPI ranks x 1 OpenMP thread
- result.ref is an ABACUS regression baseline, not an external QE/Environ reference.
- after regeneration, two independent check runs passed every comparison.
- 2026-09-29: the PCC energy moved from E_sol_el to its own E_pcc line, so esolelref
  and the new epccref were updated from a check run (old esolelref = esolelref + epccref);
  every other key is unchanged and still passes.

